From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:36:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/44] qwen27: prove the mHC merge in place, repeated and per
 row

A stream-asymmetric error is the signature of an in-place hazard, so this pins
the merge's real path at the served width: 3 rows over 4096 columns with every
row's streams distinct. In place it equals the CPU reference exactly (0.0), a
second run from the same input is byte-identical, and no row reads another's
streams. The kernel has one stream binding and reads a column's S inputs into
registers before writing its S outputs, so there is no aliasing to fix.

The first cut of this test compared an  variant that bound an
uninitialised output as the kernel's only stream input, which is why it failed:
merge cannot be out of place without a second binding, and does not need one.
---
 zig/build/qwen27.zig            |   1 +
 zig/src/families/qwen27/mhc.zig |   7 +-
 zig/tests/qwen27/mhc_alias.zig  | 175 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 zig/tests/qwen27/mhc_alias.zig

